                <pb facs="0810" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4280: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-03T21:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 3, 1922—9
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 6—11:45
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>128. Following telegram has been received from Harbin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>March 30, 5 p.m. Fifty-two cars Fengtien troops from railway zone will
                            leave Harbin today at 6:10 p.m. for Changchun. Expected 15 or 20
                            additional troop trains will be sent south within next two weeks.
                            Rumored in Harbin over-issue bank Three Provinces notes will be made
                            finance campaign.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
